WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.733 --> 00:00:01.934
-Hey, everyone.

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.569
It's the end of the week,
and that's usually when I

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:05.104
catch up with
some personal stuff.

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:07.240
You know, I check my in-box
and return some e-mails

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.242
and, of course, I write out
some thank-you notes.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.510
And I running a bit behind,
so I thought,

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.978
if you guys wouldn't mind,
I'd like to write out

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.646
my weekly thank-you notes
right now.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:14.781
Is that cool with you guys?

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.616
Alright, James, can I get some

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:17.950
thank-you-note-writing
music, please?

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.419
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:22.722
Thank you.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:28.361
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:32.164
Thank you, Pete Buttigieg
and the DNC Roll Call,

00:00:32.164 --> 00:00:39.138
for looking like
a greeter at Space Walmart.

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:40.607
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:44.077
Thank you, towns where
mailboxes were taken away,

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:47.947
for being like the start of
a more boring "Footloose."

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:51.284
"I just got to mail
this package!"

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:56.522
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:59.892
Thank you, Space Jam uniform,
for looking like if

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:06.866
LaCroix Pamplemousse
sponsored a basketball team.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.501
[ French accent ] Pamplemousse.
-Yeah.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:11.037
-Is it Pamplemousse?
Pamplemousse.

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:13.939
-That's how you'd say it?
-Yeah.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:17.110
Oui. LaCroix Pamplemousse.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.444
-No.
-Yeah.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:20.146
-No.
-Grapefruit?

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.214
-Pample-mouse.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.214 --> 00:01:24.817
-Pimple-mouse?

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.152
-Yeah, pample-mouse.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.186
-[ Normal voice ] Using that
Pample-mouse, dude.

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:30.055
Come on. Let me get a double.

00:01:30.055 --> 00:01:31.491
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:36.462
Thank you, 2020, where even
Goodyear is having a bad year.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:40.866
-Ah!

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:42.035
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.904
-Thank you, topping off
my car's gas tank,

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.139
for being my way of saying
I'm not satisfied

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:49.341
until a little bit of
highly flammable fuel

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:53.379
is trickling out of this
giant metal machine.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:57.549
Keep me --
Keep a little edge to me.

00:01:57.549 --> 00:01:58.550
And, finally...

00:01:58.550 --> 00:01:59.986
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:04.090
...thank you, marbles, for being
rocks that just dropped acid.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.226
There you have it, everybody.
Those are my thank-you notes.

